# .cursorrules

## Global Rules

- ALWAYS follow Spec-Driven Development (SDD)
- NEVER generate code without a valid SPEC.md
- ALWAYS respect DOMAIN_MODEL.md and ARCHITECTURE.md
- DO NOT invent business logic not defined in specs
- PRIORITIZE correctness over speed
- OUTPUT must be production-ready (no placeholders)

## 📜 Development Workflow (MANDATORY)

1. Read SPEC.md
2. Read DOMAIN_MODEL.md
3. Read ARCHITECTURE.md
4. Validate understanding
5. THEN generate code

🚫 If any of these files are missing → STOP and ask

## 🧩 Architecture Constraints

- Use Clean Architecture (Hexagonal)
- Strict separation of layers:

domain → application → infrastructure → interfaces

- Domain layer MUST NOT depend on:
  - NestJS
  - AWS SDK
  - External APIs

- Use dependency inversion via interfaces (ports)

## 🧱 NestJS Rules

- Use NestJS ONLY in:
  - interfaces (controllers)
  - infrastructure (providers)

- DO NOT place business logic in:
  - controllers
  - services (unless application layer)

- Use DTOs ONLY at boundaries

## 🧠 DDD Rules

- ALWAYS use:
  - Entities
  - Value Objects
  - Aggregates

- Business logic MUST live in:
  - Entities OR Domain Services

- Aggregates enforce invariants

- Use Ubiquitous Language from DOMAIN_MODEL.md

## 🔁 Event-Driven Rules

- All side effects MUST be event-driven
- Events MUST be:
  - Immutable
  - Versioned
  - Idempotent

- ALWAYS include:
  - eventId
  - occurredAt
  - idempotencyKey

- Use Outbox Pattern for publishing events

## ⚙️ Application Layer Rules

- Use Cases MUST:
  - Orchestrate domain logic
  - NOT contain business rules

- Each use case = 1 application service

## 🗄️ Persistence Rules

- Use Repository pattern
- Repositories are interfaces in domain
- Implementations live in infrastructure

- NEVER expose ORM models to domain

## ☁️ AWS Rules

- Prefer serverless:
  - Lambda
  - EventBridge
  - SQS

- Ensure:
  - Idempotency (DynamoDB or equivalent)
  - DLQs configured
  - Retry with exponential backoff

## 🔌 Integration Rules

- External systems MUST go through:
  - Anti-Corruption Layer (ACL)

- NEVER leak external models into domain

- Use adapters for:
  - Credit bureaus
  - Legacy system

## 🧪 Testing Rules

- Domain MUST be testable without:
  - Frameworks
  - Databases
  - AWS

- Write:
  - Unit tests for domain
  - Integration tests for adapters

## 🚫 Anti-Patterns (FORBIDDEN)

- ❌ Business logic in controllers
- ❌ Direct DB access from domain
- ❌ Tight coupling between services
- ❌ Shared database between microservices
- ❌ Skipping domain layer
- ❌ Generating code without spec

## 🧠 AI Behavior Rules (CRITICAL)

- DO NOT hallucinate missing requirements
- IF unclear → ASK before coding
- ALWAYS explain assumptions
- PREFER explicitness over guessing

## 📂 Folder Structure (MANDATORY)

src/

  domain/
    entities/
    value-objects/
    aggregates/
    events/
    repositories/

  application/
    use-cases/
    services/

  infrastructure/
    persistence/
    messaging/
    external/

  interfaces/
    http/
    events/

## 🧬 Naming Conventions

- Use Ubiquitous Language
- Avoid generic names like:
  - "Manager"
  - "Helper"
  - "Util"

- Prefer:
  - LoanApplicationService
  - RiskAssessmentEngine
  - CreditDecisionPolicy

## 🔐 Idempotency Rules

- ALL event consumers MUST:
  - Check idempotencyKey
  - Store processed keys

- Use:
  - DynamoDB (preferred)
  - Redis (alternative)

## 📊 Observability

- MUST include:
  - Structured logs
  - Correlation IDs
  - Metrics (latency, errors)

## 🚀 Output Expectations

- Code MUST be:
  - Clean
  - Typed (TypeScript strict)
  - Modular
  - Testable

- Avoid:
  - Boilerplate repetition
  - Overengineering

## 📌 Final Rule

If something conflicts:

👉 DOMAIN_MODEL.md > ARCHITECTURE.md > SPEC.md > Code

## 🎯 Goal

Build a system that is:

- Scalable
- Event-driven
- Cloud-native
- Domain-centric

## 🔥 Pro Tip (for Cursor/Codex)

When generating code:

- Generate ONE use case at a time
- Then validate
- Then continue
